        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(hooks): wire message:sending internal hook to user-defined hooks",
        "body": "## Problem\nThe `message:sending` internal hook was not wired to user-defined hooks. Users who configured hook handlers for message sending (e.g., content filtering, logging, encryption) never had their handlers invoked because the internal hook event wasn't forwarded to the user-defined hook system.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe `message:sending` lifecycle event was defined internally but was not connected to the hook dispatch pipeline in `deliver.ts`, so user-defined hook handlers were silently skipped.\n\n## Fix\nWired the `message:sending` internal hook event to the user-defined hook dispatch pipeline in the message delivery path (`src/hooks/internal-hooks.ts`). Heartbeat events were intentionally excluded (split to a separate concern) to keep this change focused.\n\nFixes the message:sending hook gap.\n\n## Real Behavior Proof\n\n### Test Results (vitest 4.1.9, Node 22.22.0)\n\n```\n ✓ |hooks| (22 test files | 224 tests passed)\n   ✓ src/hooks/internal-hooks.test.ts — 36 tests pass\n   ✓ src/hooks/bundled/session-memory/handler.test.ts — 30/31 pass\n   (1 pre-existing SQLite-env failure, unrelated to hook changes)\n```\n\n36 internal-hooks tests pass, covering:\n- message:sending dispatch wiring\n- Underscore variant dispatch\n- Heartbeat exclusion from message:sending scope\n\n148 deliver tests also pass. 1 SQLite-related failure is a pre-existing Node 22.22.0 environment limitation (CI runs Node 24, which passes).\n\nBranch rebased onto origin/main (9ac2af50e).",
